*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Molecule: H2O
* Basis: cc-pVDZ
* Symmetry: C2v
* Features tested: RASSCF(SA, RAS1/RAS3), MCLR(SA), ALASKA
* Responsible person: Roland Lindh
* Comments: SA-RASSCF gradients with RAS1/RAS3 orbitals and symmetry. The CI
*           code of MCLR orders the active orbitals by RAS space, the rest of
*           MCLR by symmetry; with both RAS1/RAS3 and symmetry the integrals,
*           densities and string tables were mixed up (crash in MCLR). The
*           analytical gradients agree with the numerical ones.
*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
&GATEWAY
  Coord = 3
    water
    O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
    H   0.000000   0.758602   0.504284
    H   0.000000  -0.758602   0.504284
  Basis = cc-pVDZ
  Group = X Y
  NoCD

&SEWARD

&SCF

* RAS1 and RAS3 orbitals in two irreps
&RASSCF
  nActEl = 8 2 2
  Inactive = 1 0 0 0
  Ras1 = 1 0 1 0
  Ras2 = 1 1 0 0
  Ras3 = 1 0 1 0
  CIRoot = 2 2 1
  RlxRoot = 2
  Thrs = 1.0e-11 1.0e-07 1.0e-07

&MCLR
  Threshold = 1.0e-6

&ALASKA

* RAS1 and RAS3 orbitals in a single irrep
&RASSCF
  nActEl = 8 2 2
  Inactive = 1 0 0 0
  Ras1 = 1 0 0 0
  Ras2 = 1 1 1 0
  Ras3 = 1 0 0 0
  CIRoot = 2 2 1
  RlxRoot = 2
  Thrs = 1.0e-11 1.0e-07 1.0e-07

&MCLR
  Threshold = 1.0e-6

&ALASKA
